  "_about": "Search queries for discover.py, searched on YouTube and Hacker News. \"python\" queries are searched as \"python <query>\" and a result must be about Python (Python in the title or URL, and no other language named); \"general\" queries are searched as they are and must appear in the title as a phrase (\"code review\", \"code reviews\"). A result is also kept only if its title contains every non-generic word of the query. Results show up under the Discovered tier and in Code craft. \"hubs\" are the focus sections of the site (AI agents, LangChain, Azure): their queries are searched like \"general\" ones (the phrase must be in the title), with their own hub_min_views and hub_per_query, and their results show up in that section instead of Code craft. A hub's \"topic\" is used for results from channels that aren't in channels.json.",
